 "description": "Use when the user asks where it is unusually cheap right now without naming a destination (\"kde je te\u010f levn\u011b?\", \"where is it cheap right now?\"). Rank every published rail by how its LAST measurement compares with its own tracked history, so a caller can ask 'where is it unusually cheap right now?' in one call instead of one call per destination. Each row is ONE rail, so a destination with several rails can appear once per rail with different numbers: name the rail when you cite a row. Read `searched` before interpreting a price: it is the TRIP the series was collected for (the search mode, and the fixed travel dates where there are any - a Christmas series is not the price of a summer trip), while `measured` is when we observed it; `price_covers` says what the money buys and `origins` the departure-airport cluster. Percentages are over observed days, not the calendar span. `latest_cheaper_than_pct_of_days` is the same number as `cheaper_than_pct` under a name that states its direction (higher = cheaper than more of the tracked days). `stale_rails` says how many of the rails THIS call matched are past their own freshness boundary today, with the day it was judged (`as_of`), so the caller need not subtract dates per row. Descriptive only: it ranks observations and gives no verdict. Rails with too little history are returned under `excluded`, never dropped silently. When you answer from this, say where the latest price sits in its own history and stop there: do not tell the reader to buy, book, wait, avoid or which destination to pick - the series carries no trend, volatility or live availability, so that judgement stays the reader's.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "limit": {
    "description": "optional (default 10): how many rows to return; 'matched' reports the count before the cap",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "min_history_days": {
    "description": "optional (default 30): rails measured for fewer days are listed under 'excluded'",
    "minimum": 0,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "party": {
    "description": "optional: '<adults>-<children>', e.g. '2-2' - the same A-C shape the price streams are keyed on. A well-formed party no rail carries returns `no_coverage` with the parties that exist",
    "pattern": "^(0|[1-9]\\d*)-(0|[1-9]\\d*)$",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "rail": {
    "description": "optional: restrict to one rail",
    "enum": [
     "flight",
     "package"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "sort": {
    "description": "optional (default cheapest_vs_history): 'cheapest_vs_history' ranks by the share of tracked days that were dearer; 'most_below_median' ranks by how far the last measurement sits below the median, relatively",
    "enum": [
     "cheapest_vs_history",
     "most_below_median"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
